From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/win32: scanout surfaces ask for three images

With scanout release tracking (patch 0036) an image comes back to the
app only once the host has stopped reading it, i.e. after a later image
replaced it on the display and the host released it.  With two images
(patch 0039's minimum) every acquire therefore waited for the other
image's release: wgl_test (Zink on NVK, 1280x720) ran at 1283 fps,
against 3888 fps with NVK_SCANOUT_RELEASE=0.

Report minImageCount 3 when the driver flips: one image on display, one
being released, one to draw into.  MESA_WSI_SCANOUT_MIN_IMAGES (1-8)
overrides it, for measurements.

Order: after 0039.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp
@@ -233,12 +233,17 @@ wsi_win32_surface_get_capabilities(VkIcdSurfaceBase *surf,
        */
       caps->surfaceCapabilities.minImageCount = caps->surfaceCapabilities.maxImageCount = 2;
    } else {
-      /* A scanout swapchain (Helios) shows its images in place: with one
-       * image the app would draw into the buffer on display.  Ask for two
-       * when the driver flips (apps such as Zink take minImageCount).
+      /* A scanout swapchain (Helios) shows its images in place, and with
+       * release tracking an image comes back only once the host is done
+       * with it: one on display, one released, one to draw into.  Ask for
+       * three when the driver flips (apps such as Zink take minImageCount;
+       * with two, every acquire waited for the other image's release).
+       * MESA_WSI_SCANOUT_MIN_IMAGES overrides it.
        */
       caps->surfaceCapabilities.minImageCount =
-         wsi_device->win32.scanout_flip != NULL ? 2 : 1;
+         wsi_device->win32.scanout_flip != NULL ?
+         (uint32_t)CLAMP(debug_get_num_option("MESA_WSI_SCANOUT_MIN_IMAGES", 3),
+                         1, 8) : 1;
       /* Software callbacke, there is no real maximum */
       caps->surfaceCapabilities.maxImageCount = 0;
    }
